{
  "about": "Format version 11's additions (log-format §6), one line each, following v10.json's position 22. Position 23: a `declared` type `loan` whose derived field `days` is `floor((back_on - out_on) / 1d)`, the whole days between two instants: a call of `floor` in a declaration's expressions (Appendix B). Position 24: a `declared` type `shift` whose derived field `week` is `date_bucket(on, 7d, '2026-01-05T00:00:00Z')`, the start of the window of seven days from a Monday: a call of `date_bucket` by a width (Appendix B). Position 25: a `declared` object set `long_loans` whose `where` is `in_set('lent') and days > 30`: a call of `in_set` (Appendix B; the vector holds the line, not a lake that declares `lent`). Position 26: a `migrated` event of `loan` whose migration names a relation's rename, `relation_renames`, from `lent_to` to `borrower`: the relation keeps its edges (§2.3). Position 27: a `record_upserted` of the `sys.setting` `view_kept.loan_days`, which asks for the view `loan_days` to be kept: a store that keeps no view would append beside records it never moves (§6; the vector holds the line, not a lake that declares the view); it is the setting's first version, so it carries `made`. Position 28: a `record_upserted` of the `loan` `l1` at `version` 4 that carries `made`: the write found no live record under the key, and a version above 1 says the record was retired before and is made again (§2.3; the vector holds the line, not the three events before it). Position 29: a `write_proposed` whose write is a migration of `loan` that declares `out_on` `sensitive` and changes no stored value: its preflight's report holds `restated`, what `to` states otherwise than the declaration in force (§2.4). Position 30: a `declared` type `ticket` whose required field `state` declares `initial` `new`, the value the fold fills where a write makes a record and gives the field none (§2.3): a field's `initial` in a declaration (§2.2). `negatives` holds each line written as version 10, its hash made right: a reader refuses it, since version 11 added what it carries.",
